  "verbalization": "The compound ((1S,7aR)-2,3,5,7a-Tetrahydro-1-hydroxy-1H-pyrrolizin-7-yl)methyl (2S,3S)-2,3-dihydroxy-2-(1-methylethyl)butanoate) is implicated in the relationship with Granzyme B through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of Toll-like receptor 6, which is itself targeted by Thelephantin D and 5,7-Dihydroxy-6-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-8-(3-Methylbut-2-Enyl)-4-Pentylchromen-2-One. These intermediates ultimately target Granzyme B, suggesting a chain of interactions that may involve immune response mechanisms. The evidence is supported by multiple paths, with varying confidence scores, but all converge on Granzyme B as a downstream target. The mechanisms appear to involve the activation of Toll-like receptors, leading to the production of pro-inflammatory molecules, and the subsequent targeting of Granzyme B, which is a protease involved in immune cell-mediated cytotoxicity. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential role in modulating immune responses through the activation of receptor-mediated signaling cascades."
